From: Tessel <noreply@nobaraproject.org>
Subject: [PATCH] survive a client-decorated window destroyed in its tile

With tiling and rounded window content on, destroying a window that has
no server-side decoration while it still held a tile aborted the
compositor: tiling releases the tile from view_destroy() and updates the
corner clip, which asks view_draws_own_margins(), which asserted that the
xdg_surface still exists. It is cleared just before view_destroy(). Most
clients unmap first and lose their tile on the next arrange; Discord's
updater window and any GTK window with a header bar do not.

Also skip a window shadow whose theme buffer is missing instead of
reading through a NULL pointer (seen as a segfault in
set_subtree_geometry).
---
diff --git a/src/ssd/ssd-shadow.c b/src/ssd/ssd-shadow.c
index 9ce477a..c827239 100644
--- a/src/ssd/ssd-shadow.c
+++ b/src/ssd/ssd-shadow.c
@@ -152,6 +152,15 @@ set_subtree_geometry(struct ssd_shadow_subtree *subtree,
 		int titlebar_height)
 {
 	struct theme *theme = rc.theme;
+	if (!theme->window[active].shadow_corner_top) {
+		/*
+		 * The theme has no shadow for this state (any more): a shadow
+		 * made for a window without server-side decoration outlives a
+		 * reconfigure that turned its size to zero.
+		 */
+		wlr_scene_node_set_enabled(&subtree->tree->node, false);
+		return;
+	}
 	int visible_shadow_width = theme->window[active].shadow_size;
 	/* inset in actual pixels, as a proportion of shadow width */
 	int inset = SSD_SHADOW_INSET * (double)visible_shadow_width;
diff --git a/src/xdg.c b/src/xdg.c
index 14c50e5..257eab9 100644
--- a/src/xdg.c
+++ b/src/xdg.c
@@ -847,8 +847,14 @@ view_draws_own_margins(struct view *view)
 	if (view->type != LAB_XDG_SHELL_VIEW) {
 		return false;
 	}
-	struct wlr_xdg_surface *base = xdg_toplevel_from_view(view)->base;
-	return base->initialized && (base->geometry.x > 0 || base->geometry.y > 0);
+	/*
+	 * Asked while the view is destroyed too (tiling releases its tile and
+	 * updates the corner clip), when the xdg_surface is already gone.
+	 */
+	struct wlr_xdg_surface *base =
+		((struct xdg_toplevel_view *)view)->xdg_surface;
+	return base && base->initialized
+		&& (base->geometry.x > 0 || base->geometry.y > 0);
 }
 
 static void
